{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/779667-switching-courts","id":779667,"title":"switching courts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-04T03:38:45-08:00","id":779667,"title":"switching courts","content":"okay, so the books talk on occasion that its possible to switch legacies and thereby switch courts around and go from seelie to unseelie and vice versa. my question is how does one do it. either mechanically or fluff wise? there are no actual rules for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T11:05:15-08:00","id":779954,"title":"","content":"I think it's meant to be one of those 'plenty of roleplaying and a good story' things. Mechanically, you'd just switch the Legacies around on the character sheet.<br /> <br /> As with things like a change of Nature, I'd expect there to be either a) a jarring change to the character's circumstances, or b) a quest of some kind, with personal development/transformation as either a goal or outcome.<br /> <br /> No WW/OPP games have mechanics for this kind of thing (as far as I'm aware), but it would be helpful if they did. I think intentional changes to Nature/Legacies would involve regular Willpower expenditure and changes in behaviour. Perhaps these would be backed up by successful social feats where the character demonstrates the new behaviours (for example, someone wishing to become a Trickster would have to convince others that he fulfils that role). You could use social combat rules for this and make the action an extended roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 12-04-2015, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T11:18:21-08:00","id":779966,"title":"","content":"When I first read Changeling and I saw the section saying the Courts used to switch with the season, I misunderstood and thought Changelings themselves switched courts with the seasons. It would make for an interesting game, that's for sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T16:35:23-08:00","id":780222,"title":"","content":"oh curious? Will political loyaltys automaticly shift with a change of dominant legacy?<br /> <br /> E.g. will a member of house Aili whos seelie legacy becomes dominant after a glorious victory, start to work against his allies and help the seelie enemy, or just be unusualy generous, to his inferiors, and merciful to fallen seelie foes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T13:06:54-08:00","id":781285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/779667-switching-courts?p=780222#post780222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh curious? Will political loyaltys automaticly shift with a change of dominant legacy?<br /> <br /> E.g. will a member of house Aili whos seelie legacy becomes dominant after a glorious victory, start to work against his allies and help the seelie enemy, or just be unusualy generous, to his inferiors, and merciful to fallen seelie foes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> that's a really good question. they might not be so eager to do what humans feel is the right thing considering the severity of breaking oaths, and the codes of the courts doesn't really grant a lot of options. it's possible but difficult for a Seelie fae to exist in an Unseelie house (except for Balor but they're just evil).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T18:42:45-08:00","id":781461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/779667-switching-courts?p=779966#post779966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I first read Changeling and I saw the section saying the Courts used to switch with the season, I misunderstood and thought Changelings themselves switched courts with the seasons. It would make for an interesting game, that's for sure.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've found that lots of people think this at first - including me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}